WEBVTT

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.400
And yet another war...

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:49.710
If one were to say that the history of mankind
is the history of war, few would disagree.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.710
If there is such a thing
as "progress" for mankind...

00:00:54.710 --> 00:01:02.700
...no one can say that
"progress" was not born of war.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:12.330
Perhaps man is a creature that
must fight until the last one is dead.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:19.430
In war, great amounts of blood,
tears, and knowledge are consumed...

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:25.350
...and many people's dreams
and ambitions crumble.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:33.900
In any age, there are people
who want to change the world.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:42.900
But only the people of that era can evaluate
how such ambitions changed the world.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:52.600
This is because values change with the
times, as do historians' interpretations.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:02:03.270
But a few ambitious people left their mark,
and their names were burned into history.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:09.270
These people
are called "Heroes"!

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:24.100
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:24.100
<b>OF THE</b>

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:24.100
<b>GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:10.330
Admiral, status report.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:14.240
Our fleet will arrive at
Iserlohn Fortress as scheduled.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.340
Everything is
proceeding as planned.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.340
Thank you. Request permission
to dock with the fortress.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:19.800
Yes, sir.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.150
Admiral Reinhard von Musel's
Imperial Expeditionary Fleet...

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.960
...will arrive at Imperial
time 30:27, as scheduled.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:45.700
They request
clearance to dock.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.200
At last the admiral raised in
his sister's skirts is venturing out.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.960
The Empire has hit bottom.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.270
True.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:03.100
An untalented boy is an admiral and commands a fleet because the Kaiser cares for his sister.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:07.080
Something is wrong with the
Empire's promotion standards.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:12.690
This isn't the first time favoritism
got someone promoted in the Empire.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:16.190
But it's strange for a member of
the nobility to say such a thing.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.790
Isn't that so, Baron ?

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:21.000
It would seem that the
Fleet Admiral dislikes me.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:24.700
So why do I get the privilege
of keeping you company ?

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.800
I can't stay in
the field forever.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.310
I'll have to return
to the Empire someday.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.110
Then I'll need diplomatic
connections, just like you.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.710
Let's just say that
I'm preparing for it.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:41.920
I guess I'm more important
to you than "that" Admiral.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:50.620
Why should I welcome a boy who was promoted
by a woman's power, even if she is his sister ?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:53.630
I dislike that sort of man.
He must be eliminated.

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:55.530
You must be careful
not to go too far.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:58.600
It's dangerous, since he's
favored by His Majesty.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:04.340
But at least while he's here, he's
just another admiral under my command.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.740
Isn't that right ?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:11.150
Yes, it is as you say,
Your Excellency, Fleet Admiral.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.860
Kircheis, we've arrived.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.560
Yes, so we have.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.150
But it's so small...

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:35.960
Yes, that fortress is less than a speck
of dust in the vastness of space.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.250
Yet people have been fighting
over it for decades.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:43.200
Yes. And sacrificing
millions of lives.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:45.450
We will end that.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:54.080
Yes. Not only the fight for the fortress,
but this 150 year long galactic war.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.290
Yes, soon we will
end that as well.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.290
We will.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.090
Iserlohn Fortress
is directly ahead.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:04.600
We've located possible enemy movement
near the gaseous planet Legnica.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:06.790
We're not concerned with that.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:10.200
Our first objective
is to reach the fortress.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:15.100
This fleet is too valuable to be
risked in an unnecessary battle.

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:22.110
The intercept fleet
is prepared to launch.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.510
That's not necessary.

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:29.920
It'd be faster to use the Expeditionary
Fleet than to scramble a fleet from here.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:34.020
But that fleet just
arrived from the Empire.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:36.520
They're tired from the journey,
and many of their men are inexperienced...

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.620
We're at war, Oberstein.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:44.600
They're part of the Imperial Navy.
They exist to fight.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.130
Order the Expeditionary Fleet to
head for the planet immediately.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.130
Yes, sir.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:58.340
So, are you testing the "Skirt Admiral's"
ability with this exercise ?

00:06:58.340 --> 00:06:59.840
No...

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:05.200
It's best to be rid of an uninvited
guest before he can enter.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.150
An emergency order !

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:13.960
An order from
Fleet Admiral Muckenberger...

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:18.550
Expeditionary Fleet, head immediately for the planet Legnica and destroy the enemy fleet.

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:24.360
So this is our
welcoming gift, huh ?

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:26.960
How would you
react to this order ?

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.900
You already
know my answer.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.990
What will he do ?

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:51.690
He must obey the order.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:53.390
But it's impossible.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:57.190
We've just arrived, and don't even
know what the battlefield's like.

00:07:57.190 --> 00:08:02.100
To minimize casualties, he could make
the fleet "look like" it's fighting.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.000
Look like, you say ?

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.400
Would he do that ?

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:12.610
If he does, we'll always be known as
"The staff of the Admiral in the skirt."

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:15.710
Maybe, "The staff caught
in the stockings ?"

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:22.320
The Admiral has sent detailed
information on the planet Legnica.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.320
You have thirty
minutes to review it.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:26.220
It's urgent !

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.520
Detailed information...

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:31.930
As we thought, our 
Admiral is going to fight.

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:33.430
I'd do the same.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:34.330
Me, too.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:35.600
There's no
time to lose.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.700
Okay, let's review
the information.

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:50.440
Planet Legnica, a typical
outer gaseous planet.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:53.150
The outer atmosphere is mainly
composed of helium and hydrogen.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:54.550
Helium and hydrogen ?!

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:57.950
Yes, atmospheric wind
speed is 2000 km/hr.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:02.000
In these conditions, any radar or
tracking device is almost useless.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:06.060
So it's literally
flying blind...

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:09.260
We could meet
the enemy at any time.

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:12.600
Yes, but the
enemy is blind, too.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:23.900
No sign of the enemy fleet.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.280
What's the matter ?

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:35.790
We're on red alert.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:38.990
The enemy hasn't
shown up yet.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:41.790
If you tense up now,
you'll get tired.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.290
You're used to it.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.090
Used to battles.

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:48.500
Used to it or not,
it's all the same.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:53.000
We pull the trigger and fire when
they give the order. That's all.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.600
This is my first battle.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.710
Everyone has a first time.

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:02.110
The problem is,
when does it end ?

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:05.310
But we don't decide that,
the Admiral does.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:08.210
Will we be okay ?

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:11.220
Isn't this the fleet of
"The Admiral in the skirt ?"

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:18.120
Hey ! The Commander's 
background doesn't matter to us.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:24.550
A reliable commander is one who wins
battles and takes as few losses as possible.

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:26.930
A person who understands
the men under him.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.230
How's our Commander ?

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:30.800
I've never spoken with him.

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:36.140
I'm still alive, so he
must be better than most.

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:39.600
Most of my shipmates who
went to other fleets are dead.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.050
Then I was lucky to be
assigned here, wasn't I ?

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:49.550
If you're still alive when this battle's
over, then you can say you're lucky.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:51.050
Oh, right.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:54.260
Anyway, a soldier
doesn't control his life.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.250
It all depends
on his commander.

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.650
We haven't located
the enemy fleet yet.

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:18.170
Because of electrical
interference, radar is useless.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:21.380
Haven't we located
the enemy fleet yet ?

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.080
Isn't that good, sir ?

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:29.090
Our mission is to evade the enemy,
approach Iserlohn Fortress, and attack.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:32.090
Don't we want to
avoid the enemy fleet ?

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:36.090
Commodore Yang Wenli, I am
the commander of this fleet !

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.400
I know, sir.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:40.400
But as Operations Advisor, I must...

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:44.400
Please limit your advice
to operational planning.

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:48.710
We're already on the battlefield.
Operations don't always go as planned !

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:50.910
If the enemy appears,
we'll crush them.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:51.910
Yes, sir.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:55.610
If the Commander wishes,
my job here is finished.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:56.710
It is.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:12:01.620
Now watch how an experienced
officer runs a battle !

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:04.220
Yes, sir.  I will.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:05.320
Now then...

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:06.600
...now then...

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.430
Did you argue with
the Commander again ?

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:13.250
Not really.

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:17.930
If the Commander doesn't
want my advice, then so be it.

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:22.240
I said what I should have.
I worked for my salary.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.940
So now it's
just time to watch ?

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.240
I guess that's okay.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.900
But I wouldn't want to die
under a commander like him.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:31.850
Would you like some ?

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:32.750
No.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.550
You know I don't like coffee.

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:38.050
Why do soldiers like
such disgusting mud water ?

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:42.250
I know you only like tea...

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:44.660
...but won't you try this ?

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.660
That's part of
your job, too.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.800
In that case,
I'll have some.

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:53.200
Yeah, we won't have
the guts for this sober.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:56.770
To the 2nd Fleet
of the Alliance Force...

00:12:56.770 --> 00:13:01.170
All ships rise above the clouds
and scan for the enemy fleet.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:06.780
As soon as the enemy is located,
attack and destroy them.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:09.080
Good luck to you all !

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.900
We don't even
have time to drink.

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:16.100
They're telling us to
make our work salary-worthy.

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:19.890
What lousy driving.

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.490
I can feel drunk
without drinking.

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:22.900
That's right.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:34.600
The 2nd Fleet's coming out of the clouds.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.600
Enemy ships...confirmed...confirmed !

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:35.900
What's wrong ?

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:38.210
This...

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.610
Enemy detected !

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:41.410
Enemy detected !

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:42.200
Location ?

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.110
Thermal sensors detect
many objects approaching.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.110
Enemy ships ! Enemy ships !

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:47.600
Calm down !
Where are they ?

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:49.600
There !

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:50.000
What ?!

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:55.120
Enemy ship readings.
Directly in front of us.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.000
In front of us !

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.330
Start firing.

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:06.300
Avoid colliding with the
enemy ships and open fire.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:10.540
Start firing !

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:11.640
Fire !

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:12.950
Don't worry about
crashing into them !

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.850
All ships have avoided collision.
No damage.

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:38.760
The coordinates for
regrouping, please ?

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:41.760
The current positions are fine.

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:46.300
All ships are to continue fighting
under their own initiative.

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:51.370
Damage to our
fleet is minimal.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.660
Minimal damage ?!

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.380
Of course !
The enemy's not even scratched !

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:59.680
We greatly outnumber them !
So why don't you smash into them !

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:02.080
We would win
by sheer numbers !

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.680
Who'd make a suicide
attack these days ?

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:08.000
Especially when this commander
would get credit for it.

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:20.600
Both fleets
are barely damaged.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:23.200
If they came to intercept us, why
aren't they attacking more forcefully ?

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:30.110
This is a waste of ammunition,
but it's better than wasting lives.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.700
But he doesn't
waste anything...

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.310
He's planning something.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:40.150
But that red-headed friend of his is
probably the only who can understand it.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:46.550
The weapons are causing the
temperature of the atmosphere to rise.

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:51.130
If the temperature rises,
it will cause an updraft.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:54.230
I don't like trusting
my life to the wind.

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:57.300
It's a different story
if we cause the wind.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:06.740
What's the matter ?

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:07.840
The winds have stopped.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:11.850
Possibly because of the heat
released during the battle.

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:14.850
Good. It will be easier to
fight without the winds.

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:17.750
We have the
numerical advantage.

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:19.250
The wind has stopped ?!

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:23.900
All ships ascend, immediately !

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:31.060
The enemy fleet
is ascending rapidly.

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:33.460
Are they running away,
after all this ?

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:35.370
What now ?

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:36.900
It's the wind !
A strong wind !

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:40.070
Wind velocity, 6000 km/hr.

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:42.900
Cold gasses are being pulled
into the heated air mass.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.170
Get out of the
clouds for now.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:51.900
No, sir.

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:53.980
We should ascend.

00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:56.390
All ships should leave
the surface of the planet.

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:57.390
Shut up !

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.590
If we ascend,
we'll be destroyed !

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:01.990
Can't you see that,
you inexperienced fool ?!

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:04.490
Yes, we probably
will get shot at, but...

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:05.590
No...

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:08.100
...you're the commander
of the fleet...

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:10.300
You're a pest !
Dismissed !

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:14.500
Why ascend ?

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:18.310
If I were the enemy commander,
I could wipe out this fleet with one shot.

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:18.800
Wha...?!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:22.900
What's the composition of
this planet's atmosphere ?

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:27.200
Yup, helium and hydrogen.
It would only take one match...

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:32.900
But I don't think anybody in the
enemy fleet would think of it.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:35.920
Fire a nuclear
fusion missile.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.120
At the surface of the planet ?

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.200
Precisely.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.940
Enemy missile has passed by.
No damage.

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:56.900
Bad shot !
What are they aiming for ?!

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:04.450
Oops !

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:08.250
What're you doing ?
Those're the ascent controls !

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:09.950
Oops, sorry...
I'm a little dizzy.

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.450
Our fleet has
sustained heavy losses.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:33.680
It can't be...
Such things can't...

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:34.700
Operation orders, please.

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:37.280
All ships retreat...

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.280
All ships retreat.

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:42.700
His only good order...

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.900
Enemy fleet is retreating.

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:47.600
Operation completed.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.250
We will return to
Iserlohn Fortress.

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:02.600
Beats me.

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:04.800
Have you ever seen
such a bold tactic ?

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:07.050
I'm glad he's
not my enemy.

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:12.250
It's over.

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:17.920
What's the matter...?

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:22.300
We were lucky today.

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:33.330
So there's an enemy commander
who thinks like I do.

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:36.530
If I hadn't been dizzy,
we'd be dead.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:37.730
Yeah...

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:41.440
But if I'd insisted
on ascending...

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:43.840
...the other ships might
have been saved, too.

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:45.440
Don't worry about it.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:48.440
That's the best we could do
with such a stubborn commander.

00:19:48.440 --> 00:19:49.800
On the other hand,
the enemy...

00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:56.150
I wonder who
thought of that plan.

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:58.950
The commander of
that white ship...?

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:07.150
Iserlohn Fortress, the Expeditionary
Fleet has completed its mission.

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:09.560
Requesting docking sequence.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:14.370
I can't think of any other
reasons to refuse him.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:16.460
He's quite lucky.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:19.300
But how long
will his luck last ?

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:30.880
Expeditionary Fleet, dock in sequential
order using bays 8661 through 9754.

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:31.900
Understood.

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:52.060
I'll give you credit for
defeating the enemy at Legnica.

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:55.760
But the truth is that the
weather was on your side.

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:59.960
Your victory was too dependent on luck for
it to be considered a real accomplishment.

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:06.270
Remember, in real battle,
there are no storms.

00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:10.700
Yes, sir. I plan to distinguish
myself in a real battle.

00:22:13.170 --> 00:22:14.780
Till then.

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:20.400
Don't expect another strong
wind to flip the skirt up.

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:34.800
It looks like they're offended
by my reputation here as well.

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:40.600
Any promising student or athlete
is always envied and beaten up.

00:22:40.600 --> 00:22:43.100
But an insult to your
sister is unforgivable.

00:22:43.100 --> 00:22:47.150
True. But it's useless to
challenge our foolish superiors.

00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:07.120
Okay, who'll win
the next battle ?

00:23:07.120 --> 00:23:09.730
The allies or the enemy ?
Place your bet.

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:10.830
I wonder which...

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:14.630
This one's for the enemy...

00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:14.630
...and this one's for our side.

00:23:15.050 --> 00:23:15.700
I'll take this side.

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:16.390
I'll take this one.

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:17.100
Me, too...

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:18.000
What ?

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:19.800
There's more for the enemy.

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:22.940
Do you guys plan to die ?

00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:24.240
No, Poplan.

00:23:24.240 --> 00:23:28.450
Each one plans to be the only
survivor and win all the money.

00:23:30.150 --> 00:23:35.150
If everyone does that, no one
will die and we'll end up winning.

00:23:35.150 --> 00:23:38.350
I bet on this side.

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:45.450
What are you guys doing ?

00:23:45.450 --> 00:23:47.360
Would you like
to join us, sir ?

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:48.450
Hey !

00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:51.870
Is this enough ?

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:54.460
That much...

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:56.870
Which side, sir ?

00:23:56.870 --> 00:23:59.270
Which side
should I choose ?

00:23:59.270 --> 00:24:03.300
Well, I have to look
up some things, so...

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:06.380
What should
I do with this ?

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:08.600
Put it in the one
you think will win.

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:12.900
I'm confident
I'll survive...

00:24:16.290 --> 00:24:19.390
I don't know
who will win.

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:25.200
We only lost because of
the rapid change in weather.

00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:30.000
I don't believe we made any
mistakes in executing the operation.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:33.700
Therefore, we should continue
the attack on Iserlohn Fortress.

00:24:54.410 --> 00:24:56.430
Are you studying war again ?

00:24:57.430 --> 00:24:58.930
It's a problem...

00:24:58.930 --> 00:25:01.330
Although I'm studying history...

00:25:01.330 --> 00:25:05.730
...war is on page after
page of human history.

00:25:05.730 --> 00:25:07.230
It's full of
fights and quarrels.

00:25:07.230 --> 00:25:10.100
I guess I can't deny
that I'm studying war.

00:25:15.840 --> 00:25:20.400
They decided that we
lost because of the weather.

00:25:21.750 --> 00:25:27.250
When we lose a battle they want to blame it
on bad luck, the battlefield, or on the weather.

00:25:27.250 --> 00:25:29.600
They forget that it's
humans who do the fighting.

00:25:33.260 --> 00:25:36.260
Men decide the
results of battles, huh ?

00:25:36.260 --> 00:25:40.650
Yes, and the enemy has the
commander of that white ship.

00:25:41.750 --> 00:25:44.070
There are more.

00:25:45.570 --> 00:25:48.860
"From a girl who's
in love with you..."

00:25:48.860 --> 00:25:50.660
It never ends, does it ?

00:25:50.660 --> 00:25:52.680
The fan mail ?

00:25:52.680 --> 00:25:55.880
Postage isn't free, and paper
is an important resource, too.

00:25:55.880 --> 00:25:58.080
It's hard dealing
with these fan letters.

00:25:58.080 --> 00:26:01.080
It would be cruel to throw them
away, but what can I do ?

00:26:01.080 --> 00:26:02.880
Isn't it okay ?

00:26:02.880 --> 00:26:04.690
You don't have
to avoid them.

00:26:04.690 --> 00:26:09.290
You were the hero at the
Battle of El Facil, seven years ago.

00:26:09.290 --> 00:26:11.990
That battle was
a mistake for me.

00:26:11.990 --> 00:26:16.600
Because of one victory, I'm hated by
the senior officers. I can't retire either.

00:26:16.600 --> 00:26:20.900
So the allies need
a young hero, huh ?

00:26:20.900 --> 00:26:23.700
The wages are too low
for an advertising talent.

00:26:23.700 --> 00:26:26.810
Well, I only have
to do a day's work...

00:26:26.810 --> 00:26:29.210
...in this foolish war.

00:26:29.210 --> 00:26:32.010
Even in such
a foolish war ?

00:26:32.010 --> 00:26:33.410
Don't say it...

00:26:33.410 --> 00:26:38.120
Yes, for some time,
I've been thinking...

00:26:38.120 --> 00:26:40.420
...of a way to
win this war.

00:26:40.420 --> 00:26:44.120
Although a stubborn commander
would never approve such a plan.

00:26:47.430 --> 00:26:48.730
The order to depart
has been given.

00:26:48.730 --> 00:26:54.000
This evening at 18:00, we depart
to conquer Iserlohn Fortress.

00:26:55.130 --> 00:26:58.030
Really foolish.

00:27:08.140 --> 00:27:09.850
There's been a report of
an enemy attack launch.

00:27:09.850 --> 00:27:13.250
Possible battlefield is
Iserlohn Corridor: Tiamat.

00:27:13.250 --> 00:27:16.600
Estimated enemy arrival time:
tomorrow at 09:30.

00:27:17.750 --> 00:27:25.060
All ships at Iserlohn Fortress
will launch and destroy the enemy.

00:27:25.060 --> 00:27:30.970
Men assigned to tomorrow's battle will be granted
leave inside the fortress until tomorrow, 06:00.

00:27:30.970 --> 00:27:33.470
Good luck and rest well.

00:27:34.470 --> 00:27:40.150
Although he has just arrived, I am
assigning Admiral Reinhard von Musel's...

00:27:40.150 --> 00:27:42.180
...Expeditionary Fleet to the left
wing of the attacking fleet.

00:27:42.180 --> 00:27:43.680
What...?

00:27:43.680 --> 00:27:45.280
The left wing...

00:27:45.280 --> 00:27:46.280
That's impossible...

00:27:48.080 --> 00:27:49.580
The left wing...?

00:27:49.580 --> 00:27:51.080
Is that a problem ?

00:27:51.080 --> 00:27:54.990
The left wing is the most
important position for attacking.

00:27:54.990 --> 00:27:57.490
But if you're scared,
you may decline.

00:27:57.490 --> 00:28:01.000
No, if that is your order,
I will gladly accept it, sir.

00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:09.700
Are you really serious about
giving the left wing to him ?

00:28:09.700 --> 00:28:14.600
As the commander, I decide
how important the left wing is.

00:28:30.320 --> 00:28:33.520
The battle that will take place
at Tiamat tomorrow morning...

00:28:33.520 --> 00:28:36.720
...will be named the
"4th Tiamat Battle."

00:28:36.720 --> 00:28:40.200
We wish you the best
on behalf of the Kaiser.

00:28:43.930 --> 00:28:46.830
Even the name of
the battle is planned.

00:28:46.830 --> 00:28:49.740
Maybe even the
winner's been decided.

00:28:49.740 --> 00:28:51.740
No one will win.

00:28:51.740 --> 00:28:54.940
This war's been going on for 150 years
and no one has won yet.

00:28:54.940 --> 00:28:55.940
And now...

00:28:56.340 --> 00:28:57.350
Jerk !

00:28:59.850 --> 00:29:02.950
...there's no way that
one battle will decide it.

00:29:02.950 --> 00:29:05.250
It will be
another light loss.

00:29:05.250 --> 00:29:07.150
It's almost planned.

00:29:11.760 --> 00:29:13.460
A planned action...

00:29:13.460 --> 00:29:15.350
There's one thing
that's not decided.

00:29:16.350 --> 00:29:18.460
Which of us will die.

00:29:18.460 --> 00:29:20.570
We can't find out by
reading the schedules.

00:29:21.570 --> 00:29:23.370
So, since we're
alive today...

00:29:23.370 --> 00:29:25.000
Wow, look at her !

00:29:27.160 --> 00:29:28.160
Let's go.

00:29:28.160 --> 00:29:28.970
But I'm...

00:29:28.970 --> 00:29:31.000
Don't worry about it.
You only live once.

00:29:45.990 --> 00:29:47.790
They're all shipping out tomorrow.

00:29:47.790 --> 00:29:49.490
Come on !

00:29:51.490 --> 00:29:53.100
Okay ! Okay !

00:30:10.350 --> 00:30:12.950
We take the left wing.
The most important position ?

00:30:12.950 --> 00:30:15.250
That's suspicious.

00:30:15.250 --> 00:30:19.250
What do the guys in this fortress
think of Admiral Musel ?

00:30:20.950 --> 00:30:23.250
Most of them...Enemy...

00:30:25.460 --> 00:30:26.000
Enemy...

00:30:28.650 --> 00:30:29.350
Enemy...

00:30:31.460 --> 00:30:34.460
...and ally.

00:30:40.770 --> 00:30:42.600
We'll annihilate our enemies.

00:30:46.070 --> 00:30:48.200
He'll probably
do the same.

00:30:50.880 --> 00:30:53.280
So now we're even.

00:30:53.280 --> 00:30:55.600
It's always a
draw with you.

00:30:58.370 --> 00:31:01.780
Magazines today don't even worry about
spreading dirt about the Imperial household.

00:31:01.780 --> 00:31:03.280
The Kaiser's favorite...

00:31:03.280 --> 00:31:05.390
She's the older sister
of that new admiral.

00:31:05.390 --> 00:31:08.590
I can't stand it !
She's really hot !

00:31:08.590 --> 00:31:13.690
If I was the Kaiser,
she'd sigh in my wrinkled arms.

00:31:14.690 --> 00:31:18.500
And now the younger brother
is wealthy and powerful.

00:31:18.500 --> 00:31:22.300
Thanks to his sister,
the whore !

00:31:23.300 --> 00:31:24.200
Shall we ?

00:31:24.200 --> 00:31:28.150
You'll be charged with excessive
force if you use that cue.

00:31:29.300 --> 00:31:32.130
But is he really
under there ?

00:31:32.830 --> 00:31:35.030
That blond admiral.

00:31:35.030 --> 00:31:38.330
Moron, it's a hologram.
Nothing's there !

00:31:38.330 --> 00:31:41.000
I know !
But I still wanna peek.

00:31:45.640 --> 00:31:47.040
What do you
think you're doing ?!

00:31:47.040 --> 00:31:48.200
You're asking for trouble !

00:31:50.640 --> 00:31:52.840
Asking for trouble ?
What're you talking about ?!

00:31:52.840 --> 00:31:55.940
You dishonored our admiral !

00:31:55.940 --> 00:31:59.250
So you're on that
brat's staff, huh ?!

00:32:14.560 --> 00:32:16.760
Looks like someone
beat us to it.

00:32:16.760 --> 00:32:19.060
They seem to be
from our fleet.

00:32:19.060 --> 00:32:20.160
We can't abandon them...

00:32:20.160 --> 00:32:22.000
They're family.

00:32:26.770 --> 00:32:27.700
That's enough !

00:32:31.070 --> 00:32:32.950
Please continue
the performance.

00:32:44.180 --> 00:32:47.480
Ltjg Louis Helm and
Ensign Whin Vanderberg, correct ?

00:32:47.480 --> 00:32:52.110
I'm Commander Siegfried Kircheis,
under the direct command of the Admiral.

00:32:52.110 --> 00:32:54.310
Please refrain from
any unnecessary fighting.

00:32:54.310 --> 00:32:57.450
The only one you should
fight is tomorrow's enemy.

00:32:57.450 --> 00:32:58.410
Yes, sir !

00:32:58.410 --> 00:32:58.900
But...

00:33:00.410 --> 00:33:02.110
How did you know
our names, sir ?

00:33:02.110 --> 00:33:06.320
We're just crewmen
from a cruiser...

00:33:06.320 --> 00:33:10.120
As long as you're a member of our
fleet, it should come as no surprise.

00:33:10.120 --> 00:33:12.700
Even the Admiral
knows your names.

00:33:13.420 --> 00:33:14.600
He does ?!

00:33:15.320 --> 00:33:20.400
Although he might forget the names of other commanders,
he remembers the names of the members of his fleet.

00:33:20.400 --> 00:33:24.750
That's the kind of person
Admiral Reinhard von Musel is.

00:33:25.530 --> 00:33:28.530
And the Admiral doesn't want you
to get into any unnecessary fights.

00:33:28.530 --> 00:33:31.750
Those guys aren't
worth fighting.

00:33:33.340 --> 00:33:34.640
This is the way...

00:33:34.640 --> 00:33:36.700
This is why our
fleet is strong.

00:33:48.650 --> 00:33:50.650
How are our fellow
staff officers doing ?

00:33:51.250 --> 00:33:52.650
Same as always.

00:33:53.650 --> 00:33:54.950
I see.

00:33:56.850 --> 00:33:58.560
So tomorrow is the day.{it's finally
coming, tomorrow.}

00:33:58.560 --> 00:34:01.300
Yes, tomorrow.

00:35:12.630 --> 00:35:14.130
Left wing, advance.

00:35:17.740 --> 00:35:18.750
Advance ?!

00:35:19.440 --> 00:35:21.700
Left wing fleet, advance.

00:35:32.370 --> 00:35:35.570
Why aren't the center
or right wings advancing ?

00:35:35.570 --> 00:35:37.750
If we continue, our fleet
will be a sitting duck !

00:35:38.270 --> 00:35:40.770
Will the enemy
take the bait ?

00:35:41.770 --> 00:35:45.880
As expected, the Fleet Commander
is planning to sacrifice us.

00:35:45.880 --> 00:35:47.180
What a fool.

00:35:47.180 --> 00:35:50.880
If that's what he wants,
we'll have to act accordingly.

00:35:50.880 --> 00:35:52.450
Continue advancing.

00:35:53.580 --> 00:35:57.080
But if we continue,
we'll be destroyed.

00:35:57.080 --> 00:36:00.490
Chief of Staff,
the Admiral has a plan.

00:36:00.490 --> 00:36:02.390
Surely not that plan ?!

00:36:02.390 --> 00:36:06.590
Yes, Commodore. You've done
well to figure out my plan.

00:36:06.590 --> 00:36:08.290
But isn't it too risky ?

00:36:08.290 --> 00:36:10.390
I know the risk.

00:36:10.390 --> 00:36:13.450
But is there any other
way to save the fleet ?

00:36:14.200 --> 00:36:15.450
You're right, sir.

00:36:20.400 --> 00:36:21.900
Out late last night, huh ?

00:36:22.900 --> 00:36:25.810
Never mind.
Go back to sleep.

00:36:28.810 --> 00:36:32.200
If we're going to die,
we may as well be sleeping.

00:36:38.020 --> 00:36:40.250
The enemy's left wing
is still advancing.

00:36:40.250 --> 00:36:42.220
Distance 16000.

00:36:40.920 --> 00:36:42.220
Ridiculous !

00:36:42.220 --> 00:36:44.320
Are they just stupid ?

00:36:44.320 --> 00:36:46.520
Or is this some
kind of trick ?

00:36:46.520 --> 00:36:50.450
Even if it is a trick, that
fleet's too valuable to sacrifice.

00:36:50.450 --> 00:36:53.150
The commander of the white ship
is commanding that fleet...

00:36:53.150 --> 00:36:54.750
Perhaps...

00:36:55.650 --> 00:37:00.800
If that's the case, the Imperial
Command is trying to get rid of him.

00:37:01.550 --> 00:37:02.750
Then, it's...

00:37:02.750 --> 00:37:06.750
Yes, that sort of shit
happens in the Empire, too.

00:37:14.760 --> 00:37:16.350
This is suicide !

00:37:16.350 --> 00:37:18.860
Even so, we can't
disobey an order.

00:37:18.860 --> 00:37:22.860
Damn ! Those guys from
the fortress really hate us.

00:37:22.860 --> 00:37:25.450
I should have hit
them some more.

00:37:29.370 --> 00:37:32.080
All Alliance forces, advance.

00:37:32.080 --> 00:37:34.200
Aim at the advancing fleet.

00:37:34.580 --> 00:37:38.480
As soon as the enemy is
in range, commence firing.

00:37:38.480 --> 00:37:42.050
Don't worry about damaging
the left wing fleet in front of us.

00:37:42.680 --> 00:37:46.590
Enemy left wing is 5000
from effective firing range.

00:37:43.980 --> 00:37:46.590
They'll be shot by both sides.

00:37:46.590 --> 00:37:48.890
They'll be wiped out !

00:37:48.890 --> 00:37:51.290
But he's not stopping.

00:37:51.290 --> 00:37:52.450
What's he thinking of ?

00:38:36.840 --> 00:38:39.450
The enemy is about to
enter our firing range.

00:38:39.450 --> 00:38:40.450
Stand by to fire.

00:38:41.250 --> 00:38:42.250
Now !

00:38:42.250 --> 00:38:44.450
All ships to starboard !

00:38:48.850 --> 00:38:50.550
Fleet ! Starboard turn !

00:38:50.550 --> 00:38:51.200
Starboard !

00:39:13.070 --> 00:39:14.200
What ?!

00:39:16.070 --> 00:39:18.480
What're they thinking ?!

00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:22.200
They're exposing themselves as
if they want us to shoot them.

00:39:22.780 --> 00:39:23.980
That's it.

00:39:24.680 --> 00:39:26.980
This must be a trap.
Something's going on...

00:39:26.980 --> 00:39:29.880
No, now ! Attack now !

00:39:29.880 --> 00:39:32.310
What're you saying ?!
This is a trap !

00:39:32.310 --> 00:39:34.310
We'll attack after we figure
out what they're up to !

00:39:34.310 --> 00:39:35.750
It'll be too late then !

00:39:36.610 --> 00:39:38.410
Keep quiet on
the battlefield !

00:39:38.410 --> 00:39:40.110
I'm the commander !

00:39:40.110 --> 00:39:44.210
The enemy fleet is turning.
They'll be on our port flank.

00:39:54.420 --> 00:39:56.220
Fleet, turn to port !

00:39:56.220 --> 00:39:58.030
There's no time for that !

00:39:58.030 --> 00:39:59.030
What ?

00:39:59.030 --> 00:40:01.730
The enemy's main fleet
is right in front of us !

00:40:08.130 --> 00:40:10.000
The enemy is
at close range !

00:40:11.540 --> 00:40:13.750
Commence firing.

00:40:14.340 --> 00:40:15.750
Commence firing !

00:40:44.460 --> 00:40:46.060
How did this happen ?

00:40:46.060 --> 00:40:48.350
Take a good look !

00:40:48.350 --> 00:40:50.760
The sacrificial fleet has maneuvered
into a superior position.

00:40:50.760 --> 00:40:53.750
The victim is
now the hunter.

00:40:56.890 --> 00:41:00.190
This was a very
aggressive plan, Admiral.

00:41:00.190 --> 00:41:02.190
Never again...

00:41:02.190 --> 00:41:05.500
After we win this battle, I'll never use
such a dangerous strategy again.

00:41:10.100 --> 00:41:11.800
That brat !

00:41:11.800 --> 00:41:14.200
We'll face the enemy
fleet head to head !

00:41:14.200 --> 00:41:15.500
I know.

00:41:15.500 --> 00:41:18.450
A battle of raw power.
Our only chance is to overwhelm them.

00:42:18.070 --> 00:42:23.570
Our losses are 18,651 ships
and 2,280,000 casualties.

00:42:23.570 --> 00:42:26.370
Ignoring ship losses, our
casualties are lower than theirs.

00:42:26.370 --> 00:42:28.370
The problem's not the
number of personnel left alive...

00:42:28.370 --> 00:42:29.980
...but the number of ships
still capable of fighting !

00:42:29.980 --> 00:42:33.080
We've also
lost fewer ships.

00:42:33.080 --> 00:42:36.080
But the enemy still
has an undamaged fleet.

00:42:36.080 --> 00:42:40.390
If that fleet attacks,
we'll be wiped out.

00:42:40.390 --> 00:42:45.350
Why didn't anyone attack when
that fleet crossed in front of us ?

00:42:48.290 --> 00:42:53.600
We outnumber them only
if we count that brat's fleet.

00:42:53.600 --> 00:42:58.450
But will they help us after
we used them as bait ?

00:42:59.600 --> 00:43:03.900
Imperial officers don't ask for
help from expendable forces.

00:43:03.900 --> 00:43:09.010
Even if we win, you won't
be able to avoid responsibility.

00:43:09.010 --> 00:43:11.200
A soldier does not
avoid responsibilities.

00:43:12.510 --> 00:43:15.150
We can't ask that
brat to help us.

00:43:17.510 --> 00:43:20.120
Everything will be
decided by what we do.

00:43:20.120 --> 00:43:21.120
That's correct.

00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:25.820
Our military commanders will
be displeased, even if I help them.

00:43:26.820 --> 00:43:32.350
You must know, Lord Reinhard,
that the hate of ten commanders...

00:43:32.350 --> 00:43:36.750
...is outweighed by the gratitude of the
millions of soldiers whose lives will be saved.

00:43:37.850 --> 00:43:40.550
Of course...
You're right.

00:43:41.950 --> 00:43:44.450
The left wing has
begun to attack.

00:43:45.350 --> 00:43:47.560
They're helping us ?

00:43:48.560 --> 00:43:51.200
That brat thinks
he's the cavalry.

00:43:56.650 --> 00:43:59.070
There's no time now !

00:43:59.070 --> 00:44:00.500
Do you have a plan ?

00:44:02.160 --> 00:44:06.660
A small squadron will penetrate the enemy
fleet, pretending to attack their fortress.

00:44:06.660 --> 00:44:09.750
Meanwhile, the main
fleet will escape.

00:44:10.570 --> 00:44:12.080
A decoy operation ?

00:44:12.080 --> 00:44:16.180
But the fleet going to the fortress
will almost certainly be destroyed.

00:44:16.180 --> 00:44:18.750
Who'll do the
job for us ?

00:44:21.080 --> 00:44:23.480
I'll do it.

00:44:25.490 --> 00:44:28.000
You...Commodore Yang Wenli !

00:44:30.390 --> 00:44:31.790
What's the matter ?

00:44:31.790 --> 00:44:33.290
Volunteering's not like you.

00:44:33.290 --> 00:44:35.490
Then why did
you volunteer ?

00:44:35.490 --> 00:44:38.400
We'll be wiped out
if we stay here.

00:44:38.400 --> 00:44:42.700
If I'm going to die, I'd rather
it be under your command.

00:44:42.700 --> 00:44:44.500
You think too highly of me.

00:44:44.500 --> 00:44:47.000
I only want
to pay my debts.

00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:48.400
Pay your debts ?

00:44:48.400 --> 00:44:54.930
If I'd argued more strongly at Legnica,
there might have been fewer casualties.

00:44:54.930 --> 00:45:02.130
And if I'd forced him to attack this time,
the results might not have been this bad...

00:45:02.130 --> 00:45:08.140
But would such a clever commander be tricked into accepting this kind of assignment ?

00:45:08.140 --> 00:45:10.640
If it was me...No.

00:45:10.640 --> 00:45:14.500
But I think this
plan's worth trying.

00:45:16.940 --> 00:45:20.850
The decoy fleet under the command of
Commodore Yang Wenli is departing.

00:45:20.850 --> 00:45:22.750
Good luck, everyone !

00:45:23.650 --> 00:45:25.550
What ?
Is that true ?

00:45:25.550 --> 00:45:27.050
What is it ?

00:45:27.050 --> 00:45:27.850
Yes, sir.

00:45:27.850 --> 00:45:31.650
When you say "everyone," it's only three
people aboard the cruiser Ulysses.

00:45:31.650 --> 00:45:34.060
The rest are unmanned,
remote control ships.

00:45:34.060 --> 00:45:35.450
Only three ?!

00:45:57.070 --> 00:45:58.370
I'm sorry, Captain.

00:45:58.370 --> 00:46:01.780
I wish I could
navigate this ship, but...

00:46:01.780 --> 00:46:03.780
This ship's a
temperamental beast.

00:46:03.780 --> 00:46:06.050
There's no way I could
leave it to an amateur.

00:46:06.680 --> 00:46:08.400
We've penetrated the
enemy's zone of control !

00:46:09.280 --> 00:46:10.580
Well done !

00:46:10.580 --> 00:46:12.500
Now, it's party time !

00:46:19.510 --> 00:46:23.250
The enemy's been sighted to our rear ! 
Eight thousand ships are advancing on the fortress !

00:46:24.610 --> 00:46:28.020
Oh, no ! We'll be cut
off from the fortress !

00:46:28.020 --> 00:46:30.650
Main fleet, retreat and
defend the fortress !

00:46:31.520 --> 00:46:33.020
Main fleet retreating.

00:46:34.020 --> 00:46:36.920
They've been fooled
by an enemy diversion.

00:46:36.920 --> 00:46:37.950
Fools !

00:46:39.630 --> 00:46:41.630
The enemy's main
fleet is retreating.

00:46:41.630 --> 00:46:43.130
They fell for it.

00:46:43.130 --> 00:46:45.330
All forces,
continue firing.

00:46:45.330 --> 00:46:47.130
Keep the enemy
contained, but retreat.

00:46:47.130 --> 00:46:50.250
The question is, how long
can we keep the enemy fooled ?

00:47:03.040 --> 00:47:05.550
The main force
is heavily damaged.

00:47:06.550 --> 00:47:09.650
The main fleet is
attacking the decoy.

00:47:09.650 --> 00:47:11.050
We can't abandon them.

00:47:11.050 --> 00:47:12.300
Rear Admiral Mittermeyer !

00:47:13.950 --> 00:47:17.450
It's a small thing, but please
get rid of the ghost fleet.

00:47:17.450 --> 00:47:19.760
The enemy decoy ?

00:47:19.760 --> 00:47:22.750
Twelve fast battleships
have already been dispatched.

00:47:23.460 --> 00:47:25.260
Only twelve ships ?

00:47:25.260 --> 00:47:28.260
Are any more necessary
to defeat an enemy decoy ?

00:47:29.260 --> 00:47:32.250
Of course...
Twelve is enough.

00:47:38.690 --> 00:47:39.750
A welcoming party.

00:47:49.100 --> 00:47:53.900
From the left wing fleet: Enemy fleet
attacking the fortress is a decoy.

00:47:53.900 --> 00:47:55.750
There is no need to retreat.

00:47:56.500 --> 00:47:58.950
Okay then,
let's finish them.

00:50:15.850 --> 00:50:18.250
Enemy ship !
It's located directly below us !

00:50:18.250 --> 00:50:19.350
What ?!

00:50:22.150 --> 00:50:23.650
The enemy ship
isn't firing.

00:50:23.650 --> 00:50:28.350
But if it does, the Admiral's
ship will be completely destroyed.

00:50:28.350 --> 00:50:30.260
Damn !
He's a hostage.

00:50:30.260 --> 00:50:31.150
Cease firing !

00:50:31.960 --> 00:50:33.250
Don't attack !

00:50:33.560 --> 00:50:36.650
Now's our chance to
counterattack, sir.

00:50:36.650 --> 00:50:37.650
What ?!

00:50:37.650 --> 00:50:43.850
If we attack now and destroy the enemy
flagship, the remaining fleet will slaughter us !

00:50:47.660 --> 00:50:50.770
It's quiet.
No one's attacking us.

00:50:50.770 --> 00:50:52.880
He's important.

00:50:52.880 --> 00:50:55.600
They don't want him killed.

00:51:05.990 --> 00:51:07.990
If someone fires now...

00:51:07.990 --> 00:51:09.750
It'd be hell.

00:51:22.800 --> 00:51:28.100
Kircheis, we can't give up this
victory for my life and this ship.

00:51:28.100 --> 00:51:29.900
Please wait !

00:51:29.900 --> 00:51:30.900
Attack !

00:51:31.500 --> 00:51:36.300
Sir, as far as the command of the ship
is concerned, I'm the one in charge.

00:51:37.730 --> 00:51:42.450
Admiral, please perform your
duty as fleet commander.

00:51:47.230 --> 00:51:48.740
I'm sorry.

00:51:48.740 --> 00:51:50.840
You're the captain
of this ship.

00:51:50.840 --> 00:51:55.450
I'll never interfere
with your command again.

00:51:56.740 --> 00:51:58.450
We'll proceed.

00:52:13.160 --> 00:52:16.350
There's an opening to port.

00:52:16.350 --> 00:52:18.350
All ships,
retreat immediately.

00:52:28.070 --> 00:52:29.860
Okay, let's go.

00:52:29.860 --> 00:52:32.070
Will we be attacked once
we release our hostage ?

00:52:32.070 --> 00:52:33.660
I don't know.

00:52:33.660 --> 00:52:36.970
But if I were him,
I probably wouldn't.

00:52:36.970 --> 00:52:40.650
This engagement,
the 4th Tiamat Battle, is over.

00:52:48.480 --> 00:52:49.680
The enemy is retreating.

00:52:49.680 --> 00:52:50.750
Shall we pursue ?

00:52:51.750 --> 00:52:52.750
There's no need.

00:52:52.750 --> 00:52:55.060
Pursuit would only
increase casualties.

00:52:55.060 --> 00:52:56.600
There will be more
battles in the future.

00:52:58.560 --> 00:53:01.360
This one is over.

00:53:01.360 --> 00:53:03.900
Yes, it's over.

00:53:14.820 --> 00:53:16.420
Did something happen ?

00:53:16.420 --> 00:53:17.750
Not really.

00:53:18.420 --> 00:53:21.000
We're both lucky, for now.

00:53:41.000 --> 00:53:42.650
Konev, we survived again.

00:53:43.480 --> 00:53:45.480
So, who won ?

00:53:45.480 --> 00:53:46.700
I hope we did.

00:53:46.700 --> 00:53:49.900
Oh ? Since when did
you become a patriot ?

00:53:49.900 --> 00:53:52.500
Gimme a break.  I just
don't want to lose the bet.

00:53:58.860 --> 00:54:03.460
Not only did you save the Imperial
Fleet from a disastrous situation...

00:54:03.460 --> 00:54:09.760
...but, due to your actions on the enemy
flank, you brought us almost total victory.

00:54:09.760 --> 00:54:12.390
This deserves recognition.
As the Fleet Commander, I...

00:54:12.390 --> 00:54:17.090
This is a holy war which must be continued
regardless of the consequences.

00:54:17.090 --> 00:54:21.400
The only thing that will prevent an
invasion by the evil, autocratic Empire...

00:54:21.400 --> 00:54:24.400
...is your devotion to
your mother country.

00:54:24.400 --> 00:54:31.800
Although you may die defending the Republic,
you are doing your holy duty to the citizens.

00:54:31.800 --> 00:54:36.500
As those on the front line of battle, you
are the models for all democratic citizens.

00:54:36.500 --> 00:54:42.400
I, Job Truniht, your Secretary
of Defense, am proud of you !

00:54:43.010 --> 00:54:46.510
He really is lucky.

00:54:46.510 --> 00:54:48.510
Is it just luck ?

00:54:50.110 --> 00:54:55.520
At least he's no longer the
"Admiral in the skirt..."

00:54:55.520 --> 00:54:59.420
...but he's still a
conceited blond brat.

00:55:00.820 --> 00:55:02.000
Commodore Yang Wenli !

00:55:03.520 --> 00:55:06.630
I think I misunderstood you.

00:55:06.630 --> 00:55:09.130
How about a drink
with me tonight ?

00:55:09.130 --> 00:55:12.030
I only want a
drink of good tea...

00:55:12.030 --> 00:55:13.030
...alone.

00:55:18.130 --> 00:55:20.000
I found out the name of the
commander of that cruiser.

00:55:21.740 --> 00:55:23.440
Commodore Yang Wenli.

00:55:23.440 --> 00:55:27.440
He is known as the
Hero of El Facil.

00:55:27.440 --> 00:55:30.040
Problems, Kircheis...

00:55:30.040 --> 00:55:30.840
Sir ?

00:55:30.840 --> 00:55:33.750
I had four of
them to deal with.

00:55:35.860 --> 00:55:38.860
One, how I handle the Empire.

00:55:38.860 --> 00:55:41.270
Another, my older sister.

00:55:41.270 --> 00:55:43.270
Then, my friends.

00:55:44.050 --> 00:55:46.780
Finally, the personnel
of this fleet.

00:55:47.780 --> 00:55:51.780
And now, another problem
I can't ignore has appeared.

00:55:56.370 --> 00:55:57.480
What's wrong ?

00:55:57.480 --> 00:56:00.290
Don't you like the tea ?

00:56:00.290 --> 00:56:02.090
I've learned his name.

00:56:03.090 --> 00:56:04.490
Who ?

00:56:04.490 --> 00:56:06.790
The commander of
that white ship.

00:56:06.790 --> 00:56:10.150
His name is
Reinhard von Musel.

00:56:14.100 --> 00:56:18.000
Commodore Yang Wenli.

00:56:20.800 --> 00:56:24.950
Reinhard von Musel...

00:56:38.820 --> 00:56:43.420
The light of heroes
shines like stars.

00:56:43.420 --> 00:56:46.520
This was the beginning
of two such stars.

00:56:48.020 --> 00:56:52.150
The struggle between these
two heroes has begun.

00:56:52.980 --> 00:57:03.280
<b><i>"Legend of the Galactic Heroes" The beginning...</i></b>

